
    IPW TODO LIST

For release 2.0, September 1995:

  o Complete IPW program documentation.

  o Tests for all IPW programs.

  o Hard-copy manual.

  o Reorganization of IPW directories.

  o Once again, testing on multiple platforms.

  o Color support in xv-3.10 replaces xv-3.00a.

  o new documentation format to easily generate text, hardcopy, and HTML.

For release later:

  o Write a Manual section describing color support in IPW.

  o pnm2ipw to solve the various problems with the current pbm2ipw.  This
    should also support all formats as defined by the IPW color standard.

  o Manual section for geo referencing.

  o Manual section for conversion to and from GRASS.

  o Merge in changes from BU, CREL, and UCSB.

  o Add some of the more common image processing filters.

  o Built-in RLE or other compressions.  Both a program (icompress) to add
    and remove compression, and hooks in the pixio layer to do on-the-fly
    compression and decompression.  Beware of programs that bypass the pixio
    layer.

  o Buffered I/O at the pixio layer.  Some models read and write individual
    pixels, which would be sped up by this.  If a request is larger than the
    buffer, it gets sent right through.  This would be necessary if doing
    compression.

  o Rewrite ipw.to.grass and grass.to.ipw to make better use of history
    facilities, and correctly handle global scale images.

  o Option to have fpio layer use calculations rather than LUTs.  For images
    with a large number of bits (17-32) this could make reading and writing
    feasible.

For release X, 1996:

  o X interface.  Pull multiband images into various channels then assign
    RGB to combinations of channels.  Allow arbitrary IPW commands with
    field replacement of images by channels and have the output assigned
    to other channels.  Have some builtin image processing capabilities.
    Programs to examine:  xv, xmosaic, xli, PCI, xgrass.
